# Extra .debs for the ISO's pool (binary/pool), not installed into the chroot.
#
# live-build downloads grub/shim for d-i without Recommends, but d-i's
# apt-install installs them, so grub-installer also wants os-prober
# (Recommended by grub-efi-*). Without it on the ISO, installing GRUB falls
# back to the network and fails offline.
os-prober

# cdrom installer: unlike a debian-cd ISO, live-build's pool only holds the
# bootstrap debs and lb installer's own short list (the kernel, GRUB, shim,
# busybox, lvm2 etc.), all without Recommends. Everything else d-i installs
# into the target itself must be listed here, or that step fails offline:
#
#  - zstd: base-installer, to compress the initramfs
#  - initramfs-tools: base-installer's initramfs generator. On trixie the
#    kernel's dependencies already bring it, but on forky they're
#    "dracut | initramfs-tools | linux-initramfs-tool", so only dracut lands
#    in the pool
#  - locales: localechooser, to set up the chosen locale
#  - tasksel, popularity-contest, installation-report: pkgsel
#  - task-ssh-server: tasksel only offers a task whose Key: package is
#    available, so without it "SSH server" is missing offline
#    dependencies, so a desktop can be installed offline
#  - task-xfce-desktop: likewise for "Xfce"
#  (these two are in overlays/cdrom/package-lists/desktop-tasks.list.binary,
#  which netinst doesn't get: it installs a desktop from the network mirror)
#  - the packages of tasksel's "standard system utilities" task (every
#    Priority: standard package): see standard-task.list.binary, as an "!"
#    line can't go in an #if
#
#if DEBIAN_INSTALLER cdrom
zstd
initramfs-tools
locales
tasksel
popularity-contest
installation-report
task-ssh-server
#endif
